# Generation hosted, embedding local.
#
# ── READ THIS BEFORE USING IT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This sends conversation text to a third party. The product's claim is that data stays on the
# operator's infrastructure, and with this profile that claim is narrower: what a person said reaches
# a provider in order to be extracted. That is a decision only the operator can make, and listing the
# host below is where they make it.
#
# ── WHY EMBEDDING IS LOCAL HERE, AND WHAT WAS ACTUALLY MEASURED ──────────────────────────────────
#
# Measured 2026-09-08 against this provider:
#
#   - `/v1/models` lists 428 models and no embedding model among them. That list covers generation.
#   - The `/embeddings` route serves them anyway: `qwen/qwen3-embedding-4b` answers 200 with a
#     2560-dimension vector. So hosted embedding WORKS here — a first reading of the model list said
#     otherwise and was wrong.
#
# It is local in this profile because it buys nothing to send it away. Embedding is a cheap forward
# pass over short text; hosting it adds a network hop, a per-call cost, and one more place a report's
# text is transmitted — and a report is written from what several people said.
#
# To put it on the provider instead, which is measured to work:
#
#     TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT=   (unset, so it falls back to the generation endpoint)
#     TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-embedding-4b
#
# Both are 2560 dimensions, so the two are interchangeable in the space they produce — which matters
# the day a vector column has to declare one.
#
# ── THE KEY IS NOT IN THIS FILE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Export it yourself. A credential in a file in the repository is a credential in the repository, and
# this one is committed:
#
#     export TAISCE_INFERENCE_API_KEY=<your OpenRouter key>

# ── WHAT THE CORPUS SAID ABOUT THIS MODEL, AND ABOUT THIS ROUTING ────────────────────────────────
#
# Measured 2026-09-08, nineteen fixtures three times each:
#
#   - `qwen/qwen3.8-flash` holds every contract the local model holds. Same relation on the drift
#     fixture, same refusals for negation, hedging, possibility and reported speech, same three
#     answers on tense, same refusal of a tool result that instructs the extractor. It also produced
#     `related_to` from "My sister Marta", which the local model misses.
#   - 17 of 19 cases were measured; the other two were lost to 429 after four re-sends.
#
# THE MODEL IS SUITABLE AND THIS ROUTING IS NOT, for a worker. Extraction is one call per message, and
# the shared pool answered 200 and 429 minutes apart throughout — a formation worker would be
# throttled continuously. The provider's own remedy is a key of your own added at OpenRouter, which is
# a setting on their side rather than anything this deployment can do. Treat this profile as measured
# for quality and unproven for throughput.

TAISCE_INFERENCE_ENDPOINT=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_ENDPOINT:-https://openrouter.ai/api/v1}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_EXTRACTOR_MODEL=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EXTRACTOR_MODEL:-qwen/qwen3.8-flash}

TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_ENDPOINT:-http://localhost:11434/v1}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL:-qwen3-embedding:4b-q8_0}

# BOTH hosts. Generation sends a message and embedding sends text written from several of them, so
# both are an egress and neither inherits the other's permission.
TAISCE_INFERENCE_ALLOWLIST=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_ALLOWLIST:-openrouter.ai,localhost:11434}
